# Playground against reliable public APIs — good for actually trying things out.
// postman-echo.com echoes back your request (great for checking variables / bodies).
// httpbingo.org can return any status or delay a response on demand.
// Click the "Send Request" / "Copy as curl" CodeLens above each block.

@echo = https://postman-echo.com
@bin = https://httpbingo.org
@token = dev-secret-123

### 1. The simplest request — just a method and a URL
GET https://postman-echo.com/get

### 2. Add a header and a query string, reusing a variable with {{ }}
GET {{echo}}/get?active=true
Accept: application/json

### 3. A POST with headers and an inline JSON body (echoed back under "data")
POST {{echo}}/post
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com"
}

### 4. Built-in variables — generated fresh on every send
POST {{echo}}/post
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: {{$randomUUID}}

{
  "now": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "rfc1123": "{{$datetime rfc1123}}",
  "yesterday": {{$timestamp -1 d}},
  "dice": {{$randomInt 1 6}},
  "home": "{{$processEnv HOME}}"
}

### 5. Send a body straight from a file (raw — no interpolation)
POST {{echo}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

< ./payload.json

### 6. Same file, interpolating {{variables}} inside it before sending
POST {{echo}}/post
Content-Type: application/json

<@ ./payload.json

### 7. An HTTP error response (500) — saved in history with a warning icon
GET {{bin}}/status/500

### 8. A slow response — cancel it from the progress notification, or let it time out
GET {{bin}}/delay/10
